{"id": "cand_1b", "parents": ["seed"], "cluster_ids": [], "edit_kind": "code", "micro_tests": [], "subset": null, "status": "rejected", "val_mean": 0.5888888888888888, "screen": null, "gate": {"tag": "cand_1b", "reward": 0.5888888888888888, "gate_delta": 0.08888888888888888, "gate_threshold": 0.06988134171893781, "stderr": 0.14382583584405628, "n": 10, "k_se": 1.0, "resolvable_effect_size": 0.139763, "verdict": "accept"}, "note": "indecisive (gate): SURFACE: task_template.md only (the round's best sibling and its only no-regression one). Restructured the 3-round list into an ORDERED procedure: round 1 LOOK-before-compute with a worked typed-read block, round 2 write-with-Excel-coordinate-rules, round 3 CHECK-BY-COMPARISON (count vs TARGET SIZE, one cell recomputed by a second route, row count before/after, any total the instruction names); DELETED the seed's print-back verification line and its 'reply when satisfied' exit, which every failing trace shows is what let wrong answers through. GROWN to 9 val trials via grow.py: pooled 0.5889. grow.py said promote (delta +0.0889 vs the STORED seed) but I did not book that, because the stored seed has drifted 0.10 and the briefing requires a CONCURRENT control: vs ctl_null_i0 delta -0.011 REJECT, vs ctl_null_i0r1 delta +0.122 ACCEPT, so verdict_stable is still FALSE. INCONCLUSIVE with --force because growth genuinely cannot help here -- the instability is in the REFERENCE (0.1333 between two byte-identical controls), which no number of extra candidate trials can shrink; a 2nd growth round was available and declined on that reasoning. No regressions under any reference."}
